WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.600
Every answer has a story. With Paatam, we finally get to understand it.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:20.000
I'm a teacher. Paatam reads my students' handwritten answer sheets, question by question. It suggests marks and feedback, but nothing is final until I check it and approve it. Then the parent gets the update on WhatsApp.

3
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.000
And it all happens on one grading desk.

4
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:35.600
The overview shows what's been scanned, and what's waiting for my sign-off. Six AI agents do the heavy lifting, but the final step is always the teacher. Every suggested mark waits in my review queue.

5
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.300
In Classes, I can see which concepts a whole section is struggling with.

6
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:47.000
Student Analytics tracks every child's progress, exam after exam.

7
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.600
My answer keys and rubrics guide every mark it suggests.

8
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:58.300
The exam generator drafts question papers. I edit them, and I approve them.

9
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:06.900
Our principal sees the whole school at a glance: the topics that aren't landing, and the students who need help, early.

10
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.600
Students see my approved feedback, and exactly what to practise next.

11
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:18.700
And parents get updates on WhatsApp, only after I approve them.

12
00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:29.600
From the student, to the teacher, the coordinator, the principal, and the parent, everyone sees what they need. And every assessment makes the next lesson better.

13
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:36.600
Paatam. Marks in minutes. Judgement stays human. Request a demo for your school.
